 ### Linear Interpolation on Polyhedra
-Uses linear interpolation to scan-convert the front and back faces of each polyhedron. Used for unstructured meshes. Exhibits C1 discontinuities common to linear interpolation. Linear interpolation is used because reconstruction for non-uniform sampling on unstructured meshes is not well understood and is significantly more complex than uniform sampling [S12, unofficial].
